      "side": 1,
      "message": "The duplication of all of these checks (such as \"dataFormat \u003c\u003d 0 || dataFormat \u003e\u003d IFD_FORMAT_BYTES_PER_FORMAT.length)\") is prone to bugs introduced in future refactorings. The same is true for your duplication of the skipping logic between lines 2207-2208 and 2217-2218.\n\nYou can deduplicate this logic and make it a lot less prone to bugs introduced in future by rewriting as:\n\nlong byteCount;\nboolean valid \u003d false;\nif (tag \u003d\u003d null) {\n   Log.w(TAG, \"Skip the tag entry since tag number is not defined: \" + tagNumber);\n}  else if (dataFormat \u003c\u003d 0 || dataFormat \u003e\u003d ...) {\n  Log.w(TAG, \"Skip the tag entry since data format is invalid: \" + dataFormat);\n} else {\n  byteCount \u003d (long) numberOfComponents * IFD_FORMAT_BYTES_PER_FORMAT[dataFormat];\n  if (byteCount \u003c 0 || byteCount \u003e Integer.MAX_VALUE) {\n    Log.w(TAG, \"Skip the tag entry since number of components is invalid: \" + numberOfComponents);\n  } else {\n    valid \u003d true;\n  }\n}\n\nif (!valid) {\n  dataInputStream.seek(nextEntryOffset);\n  continue;\n}\n\nIn this draft I have lumped the numberOfComponents \u003c 0 check into the byteCount check by checking for byteCount \u003c 0, which feels more natural to me.\n\nOne could get rid of the \"boolean valid\" by boxing the byteCount into a nullable Long, but that\u0027s a bit icky too.",
